{
  "requirement": "```rust,ignore\n// Defined in habeas_sdk::procedure.\npub struct AgentInput<'i, D: Graph> {\n    pub node: &'i D::NodeId,\n    pub contents: &'i D::NodeContent,\n}\n\npub trait AgentInputRenderer<D: Graph>: Send + Sync {\n    /// Present these supplied contents without fetching replacement contents.\n    fn render(&self, input: &AgentInput<'_, D>) -> Result<String, D::Error>;\n}\n```\n\nThe application supplies the renderer through agent context configuration.\nRendering errors return `ValidationError::Graph`. Neither `Graph::NodeContent`\nnor `Graph::NodeId` needs serialization or display bounds.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "I judged the tests adequate for `requirements.sdk.graph.agent-calls.judge.rendering`. I did not read the implementation. The requirement's obligations and the tests that cover them are:\n\n1. **Renderer trait and input shape.** `AgentInput` carries `node` and `contents`, and `AgentInputRenderer::render` returns `Result<String, D::Error>`. Every test implements the trait for a test graph and calls it through the SDK.\n   - `Renderer` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs` returns `Ok(input.contents.0.clone())`.\n   - `Renderer`, `FailingRenderer` and `DistinctPages` implement the trait against the SDK types.\n\n2. **Supplied contents are presented without fetching replacements.**\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs#fn[default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix]` asserts that the chat history sent to the provider contains the rendered \"source\" text. It also asserts that the recorded fingerprint value is \"source\", which is the same content that was delivered.\n   - `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[explicit_insertions_preserve_order_repetition_and_selection_snapshots]` asserts that the agent receives the exact per-node contents, in order and with repetitions. It also asserts that the graph's reads are exactly `[1, 3, 2, 3, 1]`, one read per insertion with no extra fetches.\n   - Together these show that the renderer's output is derived from the contents the SDK read and supplied.\n\n3. **The application supplies the renderer through agent context configuration.** Every marked test builds `ValidationContext::with_agent(&graph, node, &agent, &renderer)`. The agent receives the renderer's output, so the configured renderer is the one in use.\n\n4. **Rendering errors return `ValidationError::Graph`.** `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/validation.rs#fn[queued_reads_selection_and_rendering_fail_before_agent_invocation]` uses `FailingRenderer`, which returns `Err(\"render\")`.\n   - It asserts `Err(ValidationError::Graph(\"render\"))`.\n   - It asserts that no dependencies are recorded.\n   - It asserts that the agent is not invoked.\n   - The tool-agent tests in `agent.rs` go through the same `ValidationContext` renderer configuration, so I treated a separate failure test for them as unnecessary.\n\n5. **No serialization or display bounds on `NodeContent` or `NodeId`.**\n   - In `agent.rs`, `Node(u8)` is commented as having no Serde or Hash implementations, and `Contents(String)` is the `NodeContent`.\n   - `default_tool_accepts_scalar_results_and_keeps_the_exact_prefix` is marked with `requirements.sdk.graph.domain_types` and compiles and runs with these types.\n   - `contracts.rs` also has a `Node` struct commented as having no Hash, Serde or Display bounds.\n\n`src/authoring/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[authoring_keeps_the_prepared_subject_snapshot_and_concrete_version]` carries a `{test}` reference to this requirement, but it mainly checks authoring snapshots. I did not rely on it.\n\nI found no gap in the supplied tests.",
